<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ib1a49b08e344a361fd698a5f1ab300d349780a34" commit="d4d6b1805ab39d9412b4c8bf04d1686b5391fc4b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Revert &quot;REVERT-ME: Add WIP patches of aux_backlight driver&quot;  This reverts commit 00d25aad8910e0b25c9e226d78dda4d6b5ac22ea.  Revert this to put in the upstream version.  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working CQ-DEPEND=CL:440445  Change-Id: Ib1a49b08e344a361fd698a5f1ab300d349780a34 Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/546857 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="546857" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/57/546857/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I0722ffef356b5d6ccfc219744d1eb2557c04e709" commit="57d72272d79fc857644aa30c769b49ae3230215c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Drop AUX backlight enable check for backlight control  There are some panel that (1) does not support display backlight enable via AUX (2) support display backlight adjustment via AUX (3) support display backlight enable via eDP BL_ENABLE pin  The current driver required that (1) must be support to enable (2). This patch drops that requirement.  Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170523223805.46372-2-puthik@chromium.org (cherry picked from commit 49d191dd5d41ca3a6b447075d50ce5f287171f71)  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working  Change-Id: I0722ffef356b5d6ccfc219744d1eb2557c04e709 Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/501428 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="501428" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/28/501428/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I66a5c3e610cdd3d51835ae8bae3053db20573fc1" commit="1dd753084b660c74ff707dd45e9b6aa4535583e4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Don't enable backlight at setup time.  Maarten and Ville noticed that we are enabling backlight via DP aux very early in the modeset_init path via the intel_dp_aux_setup_backlight() function, since commit e7156c833903 (&quot;drm/i915: Add Backlight Control using DPCD for eDP connectors (v9)&quot;). Looks like all we need to do during _setup_backlight() is read the current brightness state instead of modifying it.  v2: Rewrote commit message.  Cc: Ville Syrjala &lt;ville.syrjala@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: Maarten Lankhorst &lt;maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Cc: Yetunde Adebisi &lt;yetundex.adebisi@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Dhinakaran Pandiyan &lt;dhinakaran.pandiyan@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Maarten Lankhorst &lt;maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Fixes: e7156c833903 (&quot;drm/i915: Add Backlight Control using DPCD for eDP connectors (v9)&quot;) Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1497384239-2965-1-git-send-email-dhinakaran.pandiyan@intel.com Signed-off-by: Ville Syrjl &lt;ville.syrjala@linux.intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit f6262bda462e81e959b80a96dac799bd9df27f73)  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working  Change-Id: I66a5c3e610cdd3d51835ae8bae3053db20573fc1 Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/546858 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="546858" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/58/546858/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I8f9bcfc64c29d99e7d92d799583cffb5db290e6a" commit="96bb55cc51e2f68d2d4e187f64fb8fb881945109" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm: Add definition for eDP backlight frequency  This patch adds the following definition - Bit mask for EDP_PWMGEN_BIT_COUNT and min/max cap   register which only use bit 0:4 - Base frequency (27 MHz) for backlight PWM frequency   generator.  Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dhinakaran Pandiyan &lt;dhinakaran.pandiyan@intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Dave Airlie &lt;airlied@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jani Nikula &lt;jani.nikula@intel.com&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170523223805.46372-5-puthik@chromium.org (cherry picked from commit 77a494a7250ce082def81a5fa67c24789ecabe0b)  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working  Change-Id: I8f9bcfc64c29d99e7d92d799583cffb5db290e6a Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/456117 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="456117" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/17/456117/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I96221608e1288ffc03a0fd9c4a658809acda4aca" commit="2eefa5820a9f7adb57f13e0ac656b4902c3dfc7b" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Set PWM divider to match desired frequency in vbt  Read desired PWM frequency from panel vbt and calculate the value for divider in DPCD address 0x724 and 0x728 to have as many bits as possible for PWM duty cyle for granularity of brightness adjustment while the frequency divisor is still within 25% of the desired value.  Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dhinakaran Pandiyan &lt;dhinakaran.pandiyan@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170622190339.142671-2-puthik@chromium.org (cherry picked from commit c03e53b030025e9243b6e5cb717ad143f3a442ce)  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working  Change-Id: I96221608e1288ffc03a0fd9c4a658809acda4aca Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/456118 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="456118" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/18/456118/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If8376b09fbf83398c40037a04ddba1035c6b71fc" commit="6e4a3f691003d05a07b6daf605da10dd8777befe" commit_message="BACKPORT: drm/i915: Add heuristic to determine better way to adjust brightness  Add heuristic to decide that AUX or PWM pin should use for backlight brightness adjustment and modify i915 param description to have auto, force disable, and force enable.  The heuristic to determine that using AUX pin is better than using PWM pin is that the panel support any of the feature list here. - Regional backlight brightness adjustment - Backlight PWM frequency set - More than 8 bits resolution of brightness level - Backlight enablement via AUX and not by BL_ENABLE pin  Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dhinakaran Pandiyan &lt;dhinakaran.pandiyan@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170622190339.142671-3-puthik@chromium.org (cherry picked from commit 560a758d39c616f83ac25ff6e0816a49ebe6401c)  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working  Change-Id: If8376b09fbf83398c40037a04ddba1035c6b71fc Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/439873 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="439873" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/439873/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I52f04b814bb4cd9df570ab59094ae974b9baec5b" commit="6bc418e4aeccabd8345d05370bfa1fd0571b84fe" commit_message="BACKPORT: drm/i915: Add option to support dynamic backlight via DPCD  This patch adds option to enable dynamic backlight for eDP panel that supports this feature via DPCD register and set minimum / maximum brightness to 0% and 100% of the normal brightness.  Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dhinakaran Pandiyan &lt;dhinakaran.pandiyan@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20170622190339.142671-4-puthik@chromium.org (cherry picked from commit ae25eceab616d16a07bcaa434b84463d58a3bdc3)  BUG=b:35647498, b:35648322 TEST=backlight adjustment / CABC working  Change-Id: I52f04b814bb4cd9df570ab59094ae974b9baec5b Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik